      <h2>Designed for North Texas Conditions</h2>
      <p>Fort Worth sits in hail country, so we often recommend standing-seam metal roofs — which suit the western look anyway — or impact-rated shingles. Clay soils in much of Tarrant County expand and contract with rain and drought, so foundations are engineered for movement and the site is graded to shed water. West of the city, rocky ground and long utility runs are common on acreage, and well and septic systems may be part of the budget.</p>
      <p>Inside, we design for heat first: shaded glass, porches on the west and south sides, tight insulation and efficient heat pumps. For a THOW or park model parked in the open, we add skirting and tie-downs for wind.</p>

      <h2>Western Style, Small Footprint</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Board-and-batten, corrugated metal or limestone accents</li>
