        <li>Lofts for sleeping or storage under a steep gable</li>
        <li>Mudrooms and outdoor showers for working ranch life</li>
        <li>Large windows framed toward pasture and sunset views</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Browse our <a href="/home-designs/">house designs</a> for layout ideas, or start fresh with our <a href="/tiny-house-design-services/">tiny house design services</a>.</p>

      <h2>Communities We Serve Near Fort Worth</h2>
      <p>Cowboy Tiny Homes builds across <strong>Tarrant County</strong> — Fort Worth, Arlington, Keller, Southlake, Haltom City, Benbrook and Saginaw — as well as Weatherford, Aledo, Springtown and Azle in <strong>Parker County</strong>, and Burleson, Cleburne and Joshua in <strong>Johnson County</strong>. We also take projects in Wise, Hood and Denton counties. Building on the east side of the metroplex? See <a href="/tiny-home-builders-dallas/">tiny house builders in Dallas</a>.</p>

      <h2>Budgeting a Fort Worth Tiny Home</h2>
      <p>Costs depend most on home type, size, finishes and site work — and on acreage, utilities can be a big line item. Get a fast estimate with the <a href="/tools/tiny-home-cost-calculator/">tiny home cost calculator</a>, compare payment options with the <a href="/tools/tiny-home-loan-calculator/">tiny home loan calculator</a>, and if you are adding a rentable casita, check the <a href="/tools/adu-rental-income-calculator/">ADU rental income calculator</a>.</p>
